# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=host spec=priest:discipline style=wander
# size=25 difficulty=heroic view=1280x800 save=fresh. `boss=host` is a
# coverage label only -- `evening` steers at no boss, the walk starts at the
# door same as any other.
#
# A fresh save only opens Bonegrinder 10-normal by default, so
# #b=marrow&s=25&h=1 unlocks the whole chain up to 25-heroic before backing
# out to a real RAID -> WALK IN at the door (direction.md's 2026-09-26
# driver-lesson recipe), rather than landing on the invite's own single-fight
# "visiting" framing.
#
# What no session has done before, checked against sessions.jsonl and
# direction.md first: `wander` has been run inside `evening` before (druid:
# guardian, 10-normal, stalled THE VIGIL) but never at 25-heroic, and no
# healer spec has ever been given a `wander`-style evening at all -- every
# prior evening healer used `idle` (paladin:holy) or was a dps/tank. `wander`
# presses a random ability slot round-robin with no target awareness, so a
# discipline priest under it will cast heals and shields at whatever the
# round-robin lands on, not at whoever is low -- direction.md's existing
# wander note (holy paladin at Bloodgorged) already showed a healer under
# this style spending most of a fight "Out of range" and healing least of
# anyone on the board. This is the first chance to see whether that holds at
# heroic/25, where direction.md's own line 1 has only ever shown idle/good
# healers, never a wandering one, carrying a raid.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
tap next
tap class:priest:discipline
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start

evening wander 260 6
state
shot end
says
bill
